# demonsilver.lic
=begin
      author: Fizzleworth (fork of silverDemon.lic 0.0.2 by Dalazashel)
        name: demonsilver
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, demon, minor summoning, silver, encumbrance
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.2
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Your minor demon (Minor Summoning, 725) can carry silver for you. Out hunting, the coins you
  loot go to the demon so they don't weigh you down, and at the end of the hunt you take them back
  so the rest's ;eloot sell banks them. It's the reverse of ;demonmana, which fills the demon while
  you rest and empties it mid-hunt.

    ;demonsilver              give it all the silver you're carrying
    ;demonsilver 500          give it 500 (;demonsilver give 500 is the same)
    ;demonsilver get          take back everything it holds
    ;demonsilver get 500      take back 500
    ;demonsilver help

  The hunt part is ;demonsilver_watch (Fizzleworth-prep starts it). Each "You gather the remaining
  N coins." from a corpse while bigshot runs becomes a ;demonsilver give N. Fizzleworth-prerest runs
  ;demonsilver get before eherbs and the eloot sell. summond also runs it before it sends a demon
  back, because a demon takes whatever it holds through the rift with it.
    ;vars set demonsilver=off   the watcher stops giving (get still works)
    ;vars set demonsilver=on    back on (unset counts as on)

  Changed from silverDemon.lic:
  - It finds the demon with a silent TELL MDEMON RETURN, the same way demonmana does, which also
    calls it back if it wandered off. silverDemon's `tell md to follow` regex missed the "already
    following" and "begins to travel" replies.
  - GIVE goes to #id, never to a bare word, because a word can also match a player's name
    ("give glah 20000" handed Glahnvis 20,000 coins on 06/19).
  - It understands what the demon answers, including when it's full, and remembers how much this
    session gave it.

  Game text, all from Fizzleworth's logs (06/2026 to 11/09):
    give raven 2000       A large glossy raven grabs 2000 coins from you.
                          A humming vultite verlok'cina grabs 1878 coins from you, but cannot hold any more.
                          But you don't have that many coins.
    give mdem 200         What is it you're trying to give?   (GIVE takes no mdemon keyword)
    tell mdem give 1000   Your copper verlok'asha hands you 1000 silvers.
                          Your vultite verlok'cina does not have that much so it hands you 2800 silvers.
                          Your copper verlok'asha doesn't have any coins.
                          How do you expect your vaalorn verlok'cina to give you anything if it isn't in the same room as you?
    give #<id> <n>        A large glossy raven grabs 420 coins from you.   (15 times on 11/13)
                          What is it you're trying to give?   (the demon had just been left a room behind)
    tell mdem give 10000  Your glossy raven does not have that much so it hands you 3300 silvers.  (11/13)
  Neither command has a roundtime (07/11 mid-fight, 07/28 between go2 steps). How much a demon holds
  varies: a vultite verlok'cina 2,800 (07/11, 07/15), Fizzleworth's raven-disguised verlok'asha 3,300
  (11/13). The "cannot hold any more" reply says when it's full, and the rest stays with you.

  v0.2 (11/13, after the first live hunts): the end-of-hunt get waits 120s (not 60) for a demon left
  behind on the walk home; GIVE and TELL ... GIVE no longer go through dothistimeout (it re-sent a give
  that had already worked when another script's command got "Wait 1 sec."); a give that finds the
  demon gone counts as "not here, try again" instead of an error; the noun fallback is gone.
=end

module Demonsilver
  # Methods rather than constants: Lich keeps a script's constants between runs, so an edited
  # constant would only take effect after a relog.
  # 11/13 21:48: go2 took the climbs and jumps home from the Labyrinth, which the raven can't follow;
  # it reached the Trophy Room 72s after the prerest's get started waiting, and a 60s wait missed it.
  def self.arrive_wait
    120   # get: seconds to wait for a demon that's on its way back
  end

  def self.recall_every
    15    # ...repeating TELL MDEMON RETURN this often (an imp needed it, 11/01)
  end

  def self.get_ask
    10_000  # get with no amount asks for this much and is handed what the demon has
  end

  def self.return_reply
    /already here!|acknowledges your order|interfering with your|You have no minor demon at this time/i
  end

  # TELL MDEMON RETURN replies carry the demon's link: id, noun (an illusion's noun when it's
  # disguised) and the name it goes by now.
  def self.demon_link
    %r{(?:[Bb]ut your|Your|your) <pushBold/><a exist="(\d+)" noun="([\w,'-]+)">([\w\-' ]+)</a><popBold/>}
  end

  def self.grabbed
    /grabs ([\d,]+) coins from you(, but cannot hold any more)?/
  end

  def self.too_few
    /you don't have that many coins/i
  end

  # The demon isn't in the room after all: bigshot stepped on just as the give went out
  # (11/13 21:08:52 and 21:48:07, both a second after eloot finished).
  def self.not_found
    /What is it you're trying to give|could not find what you were referring/i
  end

  def self.wait_line
    /(?:\.\.\. ?wait|\AWait) (\d+) sec|\ASorry, you may only type ahead/
  end

  # Anchored on "Your": a bank teller or a pawnbroker also "hands you" silvers.
  def self.handed
    /^Your .+ hands you ([\d,]+) silvers/
  end

  def self.short
    /does not have that much/
  end

  def self.empty
    /^Your .+ doesn't have any coins/
  end

  def self.away
    /^How do you expect your .+ isn't in the same room as you/
  end

  # What this Lich session knows the demon holds of yours: { id:, coins:, full: }. A different
  # demon (new id, or a relog: ids change at login) starts out unknown.
  def self.held_for(id)
    h = $demonsilver_held
    h.is_a?(Hash) && h[:id].to_s == id.to_s ? h : nil
  end

  def self.record(id, coins, full)
    $demonsilver_held = { id: id.to_s, coins: [coins.to_i, 0].max, full: full ? true : false }
  end

  # => { id:, noun:, name:, here:, coming: }, :none (no demon at all) or nil (no answer).
  def self.lookup
    text = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("tell mdemon return", return_reply).to_a.join("\n")
    return :none if text =~ /no minor demon/i
    return nil unless text =~ demon_link

    { id: $1, noun: $2, name: $3,
      here: text.include?("already here!"), coming: text.include?("begins to travel") }
  end

  def self.room_objects
    Array(GameObj.npcs) + Array(GameObj.loot) + Array(GameObj.room_desc)
  end

  def self.in_room?(id)
    room_objects.any? { |o| o.id.to_s == id.to_s }
  end

  def self.no_demon(d, quiet)
    $demonsilver_last = (d == :none ? :none : :away)
    return if quiet

    echo(d == :none ? "you have no minor demon." : "no answer to TELL MDEMON RETURN.")
  end

  # Waits up to `secs` for a demon that was told to come back, calling it again every so often.
  def self.wait_for(d, secs)
    echo "your #{d[:name]} isn't here -- waiting up to #{secs}s for it."
    secs.times do |i|
      return true if in_room?(d[:id])
      if i > 0 && (i % recall_every).zero?
        again = Lich::Util.quiet_command_xml("tell mdemon return", return_reply).to_a.join("\n")
        return true if again.include?("already here!")
      end
      sleep 1
    end
    in_room?(d[:id])
  end

  # Sends `cmd` and returns the first line matching `ours` (or nil). Not dothistimeout: that re-sends
  # on ANY "Wait N sec." it reads, even one meant for another script's command. 11/13 21:43:51 the
  # attack script's `prep 710` got "Wait 1 sec.", dothistimeout took it for the give's, and the give
  # (which had already worked) went out twice. Here a Wait line only leads to one re-send, and only
  # if no reply of ours turns up by the time it says.
  def self.ask(cmd, ours, secs = 4)
    Script.current.clear
    put cmd
    deadline = Time.now.to_f + secs
    resend_at = nil
    resent = false
    while Time.now.to_f < deadline
      line = get?
      if line.nil?
        if resend_at && !resent && Time.now.to_f >= resend_at
          resent = true
          put cmd
          deadline = Time.now.to_f + secs
        end
        sleep 0.1
        next
      end
      return line if line =~ ours
      if !resent && !resend_at && line =~ wait_line
        resend_at = Time.now.to_f + [$1.to_i, 1].max + 0.5
        deadline = [deadline, resend_at + secs].max
      end
    end
    nil
  end

  # By #id only (worked 15 times on 11/13), never a bare word, which can match a player's name.
  def self.give_to(d, amount)
    ask("give ##{d[:id]} #{amount}", Regexp.union(grabbed, too_few, not_found, /^You give /)).to_s
  end

  # Sets $demonsilver_last to the coins the demon took (an Integer, 0 when there was nothing to
  # give), or :away / :none / :full / nil (failed) -- demonsilver_watch reads it.
  def self.give(amount, quiet: false)
    $demonsilver_last = nil
    return echo("you're dead.") if dead?

    d = lookup
    return no_demon(d, quiet) unless d.is_a?(Hash)

    unless d[:here]
      $demonsilver_last = :away
      return if quiet

      return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here#{d[:coming] ? ' (told it to come back)' : ''} -- try again when it is.")
    end

    h = held_for(d[:id])
    if h && h[:full]
      $demonsilver_last = :full
      return quiet ? nil : echo("your #{d[:name]} can't hold any more (#{h[:coins]} of yours). ;demonsilver get empties it.")
    end

    amount ||= Lich::Util.silver_count
    if amount.to_i <= 0
      $demonsilver_last = 0
      return quiet ? nil : echo("you have no silver on you.")
    end

    2.times do
      waitrt?
      r = give_to(d, amount)
      if r =~ grabbed
        n = $1.delete(',').to_i
        full = !$2.nil?
        record(d[:id], (h ? h[:coins] : 0) + n, full)
        $demonsilver_last = n
        if full
          echo "your #{d[:name]} took #{n} silver and can't hold any more -- the rest stays with you."
        elsif !quiet
          echo "your #{d[:name]} took #{n} silver#{h ? " (#{h[:coins] + n} of yours now)" : ''}."
        end
        return
      elsif r =~ too_few
        have = Lich::Util.silver_count
        if have > 0 && have < amount
          amount = have
          next
        end
        $demonsilver_last = 0
        return quiet ? nil : echo("you don't have #{amount} silver on you.")
      elsif r =~ not_found
        $demonsilver_last = :away
        return quiet ? nil : echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't in the room after all -- try again when it is.")
      elsif r =~ /^You give /
        $demonsilver_last = nil
        return echo("*** that GIVE went to someone else: #{r.strip}")
      else
        $demonsilver_last = nil
        return echo("give said: #{r.strip.empty? ? 'nothing' : r.strip[0, 140]}")
      end
    end
  end

  def self.get(amount)
    return echo("you're dead.") if dead?

    # The end of the hunt: loot the watcher hasn't handed over yet stays with you for the bank.
    $demonsilver_pending = 0 if amount.nil?
    d = lookup
    return no_demon(d, false) unless d.is_a?(Hash)

    h = held_for(d[:id])
    unless d[:here]
      # Nothing of ours on it: don't hold up the rest waiting for it.
      return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here, and it holds none of your silver.") if h && h[:coins].zero?
      unless d[:coming] && wait_for(d, arrive_wait)
        return echo("your #{d[:name]} isn't here, so it keeps your silver for now. ;demonsilver get later.")
      end
    end

    total = 0
    emptied = false
    4.times do
      want = amount ? amount - total : get_ask
      break if want <= 0

      waitrt?
      r = ask("tell mdem give #{want}", Regexp.union(handed, empty, away)).to_s
      if r =~ handed
        n = $1.delete(',').to_i
        total += n
        emptied = true if r =~ short || (amount.nil? && n < want)
        break if emptied || amount
      elsif r =~ empty
        emptied = true
        break
      elsif r =~ away
        echo "your #{d[:name]} wandered off before it could hand anything over."
        break
      else
        echo "tell mdem give said: #{r.strip.empty? ? 'nothing' : r.strip[0, 140]}"
        break
      end
    end

    left = emptied ? 0 : [(h ? h[:coins] : 0) - total, 0].max
    record(d[:id], left, false) if emptied || total > 0 || h
    if total > 0
      echo "got #{total} silver back from your #{d[:name]}."
    elsif emptied
      echo "your #{d[:name]} had no silver."
    end
  end

  def self.help
    n = "#{$lich_char}#{Script.current.name}"
    respond ""
    respond "  #{n}              give your minor demon all the silver you're carrying"
    respond "  #{n} 500          give it 500 (#{n} give 500 is the same)"
    respond "  #{n} get          take back everything it holds"
    respond "  #{n} get 500      take back 500"
    respond ""
    respond "  Out hunting, ;demonsilver_watch gives it the silver from each corpse you loot (Fizzleworth-prep"
    respond "  starts it), and Fizzleworth-prerest takes it all back. ;vars set demonsilver=off stops the watcher."
    respond ""
  end

  def self.amount_arg(word)
    return nil if word.nil? || word.empty?
    return nil unless word =~ /\A\d[\d,]*\z/

    n = word.delete(',').to_i
    n > 0 ? n : nil
  end

  def self.main
    words = Script.current.vars[1..].to_a.map(&:to_s)
    quiet = !words.delete('--quiet').nil?
    cmd = words[0].to_s.downcase
    case cmd
    when '', 'give'
      if words[1] && !amount_arg(words[1])
        return echo("not an amount: #{words[1]}")
      end
      give(amount_arg(words[1]), quiet: quiet)
    when /\A\d[\d,]*\z/
      give(amount_arg(cmd), quiet: quiet)
    when 'get'
      if words[1] && !amount_arg(words[1])
        return echo("not an amount: #{words[1]}")
      end
      get(amount_arg(words[1]))
    else
      help
    end
  end
end

Demonsilver.main
